1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,850
Two official records disagree.

2
00:00:01,850 --> 00:00:04,008
Which number goes to the regulator?

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,008
The field is not the whole story.

4
00:00:08,008 --> 00:00:12,512
Accountability means reconstructing which
source supported it, and staying

5
00:00:12,512 --> 00:00:14,520
answerable when records disagree.

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:21,200
KRISEVA ATTEST is a research-stage
prototype: one fictional fund manager,

7
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:23,907
three synthetic sources, three fields.

8
00:00:23,907 --> 00:00:27,112
It files nothing and has no IFSCA
connection.

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,182
The administrator statement shows
twenty-five million US dollars.

10
00:00:32,182 --> 00:00:35,528
The subscription register shows
twenty-four million.

11
00:00:35,528 --> 00:00:38,938
ATTEST preserves both figures and proposes
no winner.

12
00:00:38,938 --> 00:00:44,408
A named reviewer selects the administrator
source, types a review reason, and submits

13
00:00:44,408 --> 00:00:45,244
the decision.

14
00:00:45,244 --> 00:00:48,976
Both candidates stay visible, before and
after the choice.

15
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,166
A second named role, the Principal
Officer, confirms the record.

16
00:00:54,166 --> 00:00:58,919
The receipt keeps the reviewer, the
officer, the reason, and a timestamp.

17
00:00:58,919 --> 00:01:03,736
An integrity digest fingerprints the
manifest so the record cannot quietly

18
00:01:03,736 --> 00:01:05,168
change after the fact.

19
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,490
This is synthetic data.

20
00:01:07,490 --> 00:01:10,794
Nothing here files anything or reaches a
regulator.

21
00:01:10,794 --> 00:01:15,264
The harness is built and tested before any
model ever goes inside it.

22
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:19,957
This demo used synthetic data.

23
00:01:19,957 --> 00:01:24,198
It is not a regulatory filing, and the
narration was synthesized.

24
00:01:24,198 --> 00:01:28,896
Next is practitioner testing with real
fund managers and administrators.
